'''David C. Schmittlein''' (April 15, 1955 – March 13, 2025) was an American academic administrator who served as the John C Head III [[Dean (education)|Dean]] and Professor of Marketing at the [[MIT Sloan School of Management]]<ref name="MITSloanCIO">{{cite news|url=http://www.mitcio.com/david-schmittlein-mit-sloan-school-management|title=MIT Sloan CIO Symposium: David Schmittlein|work=[[MIT Sloan CIO Symposium]]|date=2015-05-18|accessdate=2015-05-30}}</ref>  for 17 years. He was appointed on August 27, 2007 and served until stepping down on February 5, 2024.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|title=MIT picks an outsider to lead Sloan School - The Boston Globe|url=https://archive.boston.com/business/articles/2007/08/28/mit_picks_an_outsider_to_lead_sloan_school/|access-date=2021-12-31|website=archive.boston.com|language=en}}</ref><ref>https://orgchart.mit.edu/letters/dean-david-schmittlein-step-down</ref> Prior to joining MIT, Schmittlein was the Ira A. Lipman Professor and Professor of Marketing at the [[Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania]].

== Background ==
Schmittlein was a native of [[Northampton, Massachusetts]].<ref name=":0"/> He earned a [[Bachelor of Arts|B.A.]] in mathematics from [[Brown University]] in 1977 and received his [[M.Phil.]] and [[Doctor of Philosophy|Ph.D.]] in business from [[Columbia Business School]] in 1979 and 1980, respectively.

Schmittlein died on March 13, 2025, at the age of 69.<ref>{{cite web |author=<!-- not stated --> |date=March 13, 2025 |title= David C. Schmittlein |url= https://www.currentobituary.com/obit/291752 |website= currentobituary.com |location= |publisher= |access-date=March 17, 2025}}</ref>

== Career ==
Schmittlein was formerly a professor of marketing at the [[Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania|Wharton School]] of the [[University of Pennsylvania]] and chair of the editorial board for [[Wharton School Publishing]]. He joined MIT in 2007 as the first dean of the Sloan School of Management since 1966 to be recruited from outside the university.<ref name=":0"/> On January 30, 2024, he announced he was stepping down from his role in order to attend to a personal health concern.

In 2015, Schmittlein joined the board of CIGNEX Datamatics, an [[open-source software]] company based in [[Santa Clara, California]].<ref>{{Cite web |url= http://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/announcements/others/ms-cignex-datamatics-inc-subsidiary-of-the-datamatics-global-services-limited-appoints-dr-david-c-schmittlein-as-a-director/article6853065.ece| title=M/s. Cignex Datamatics. Inc.. subsidiary of the Datamatics Global Services Limited appoints Dr. David C. Schmittlein as a Director |date= February 3, 2015 |publisher= Hindu Business Line |accessdate= March 24, 2017 }}</ref>

